# Regulatory Compliance Rules

This is regulated medical device software (SaMD) for the NCDA.
All code generation MUST comply with IEC 62304, ISO 13485, and ISO 14971.

## Traceability (IEC 62304)

- Every design control traces: User Need -> Design Input -> Design Output -> Verification.
- Traceability is modelled as Neo4j relationships (`[:TRACES_TO]`), not metadata fields.
- No orphan requirements. Every node in the traceability chain must be linked.
- All AI-generated content MUST carry `generated_by` provenance.

## Human Approval (MANDATORY)

- Human approval is REQUIRED before any AI-generated content enters the official audit.
- Approval creates an `(:Approval)` node: `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `reason`.
- Approval nodes are NEVER modified after creation. Append-only.

## Risk Management (ISO 14971)

- Risks are `(:Risk)` nodes linked to design controls via `[:MITIGATES]`.
- Every risk has: `hazardous_situation`, `severity`, `probability`, `risk_level`, `mitigation`.
- Unacceptable risks MUST generate additional design inputs (risk-mitigating controls).
- Risk analysis is a workflow step, not a manual afterthought.

## Audit Trail (MANDATORY)

- Every state-changing operation creates a `(:Change)` node in Neo4j.
- Change nodes record: `changed_by`, `changed_at`, `field`, `old_value`, `new_value`.
- `(:Change)` nodes are append-only. NEVER update or delete them.
- `(:Job)` and `(:JobStep)` nodes are append-only for status transitions (never go backwards).
- Jobs are NEVER deleted. They form part of the audit trail.

## Immutability Rules

- `(:Approval)` nodes: NEVER modified after creation.
- `(:Change)` nodes: NEVER modified after creation.
- `(:AIInvocation)` nodes: NEVER modified after creation.
- `(:WorkflowDefinition)` with status `active`: immutable. Create a new version to change.
- Versioning: superseded resources linked via `[:SUPERSEDED_BY]` relationships.
